  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nNortheasterly flow will knock temperatures down on Monday with\nhighs in the mid 80s (max heat index around 90) northeast to \nthe mid 90s (max heat index around 100) southwest). However,\nconvection over the southern CWA may lead to changes in these\ntemperature expectations. \n\nWarmer Tuesday with the return of southerly flow. Look for highs\nin the low 90s to around 100 (warmest southwest) with max heat\nindex values in the upper 90s to mid 100s. Wednesday may be a\ncouple degrees warmer. However, NBM spread is pretty high so\nexpect changes to these forecasts.\n\nLook for a 30-40% chance of showers and storms Wednesday night\nas a cold front passes through, followed by potentially cooler\nweather late week. Models show a temperature gradient just to\nthe southwest, so the forecast may change substantially with\nsmall shifts in guidance, but we are currently shown by ensemble\nmeans to be on the \"cold\" side of the gradient. This puts the\nhighs in the mid 80s northeast to the mid 90s southwest in the\nofficial forecast.",
